OL,3,AKing praises Strait of Hormuz peace
OL,4,Aefforts at glittering banquet
OL,5,
OL,6,FKing Charles spoke Arabic as he
OL,7,Fwelcomed the Sultan of Oman at a
OL,8,Fglittering state banquet in Windsor
OL,9,FCastle.
OL,11,FOman is a key Middle Eastern partner of
OL,12,Fthe UK, and one of the countries along
OL,13,Fthe Strait of Hormuz, with the red
OL,14,Fcarpet rolled out for Sultan Haitham
OL,15,Fbin Tarik Al Said.
OL,17,FThe King's banquet speech praised the
OL,18,Fcountry's "noble efforts in trying to
OL,19,Fkeep open one of the world's most
OL,20,Fimportant shipping routes".
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
